    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d667">

                <pb facs="0851" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg843"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.5151/247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-28T23:00:00+09:00">July 28, 1941—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 28—11:48 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1111. Embassy’s 1108, July 28, 8 p.m.,<anchor n="11" xml:id="d667-f1"/> numbered
                    paragraph 4. The attention of the Department is called to the fact that, whereas
                    the American Government’s order freezing Japanese assets restricts monthly
                    expenditures of Japanese nationals to $500, the Japanese ordinance provides for
                    a sum of only 500 yen.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
